Subject: Disable asm.js translation while retaining JavaScript fallback

Base: rusty_v8 v0.106.0, V8 12.9.202.13
(V8 revision 245ce17ed8483e6bc3de7f668635f46c5bfdd8a0).

Moonrun loads Wasm directly and does not need asm.js-to-Wasm translation.
Make validate_asm a compile-time false constant, following no-js-optimizer.patch.
UseAsmWasm then rejects specialization before the compilation job is created,
allowing ordinary C++ optimization and final-link dead stripping to discard the
asm.js parser and scanner. A mutable flag defaulting to false would retain that
compilation path. This does not require C++ LTO.

JavaScript with a "use asm" directive still executes as ordinary JavaScript.
Wasm compilation, GC and Inspector remain enabled; the separate RegExp patch
removes that library. Keep source lists
and implementations intact: unused code can remain in the archive, and this
does not reduce its compilation cost. InstantiateAsmJs and related runtime
metadata remain; this is not complete removal of every asm.js component.

The consumer checks valid asm.js arithmetic and verifies that its module was
not specialized, alongside the existing baseline/optimizing Wasm tests. On a
V8 upgrade, recheck UseAsmWasm, compilation-job callers and flag implications;
new references can retain translation code. Measure the final executable on
each linker rather than treating a passing runtime test as evidence of size.

--- a/v8/src/flags/flag-definitions.h
+++ b/v8/src/flags/flag-definitions.h
@@ -1641,7 +1641,7 @@
     experimental_wasm_pgo_from_file, false,
     "experimental: read and use Wasm PGO data from a local file (for testing)")
 
-DEFINE_BOOL(validate_asm, true,
+DEFINE_BOOL_READONLY(validate_asm, false,
             "validate asm.js modules and translate them to Wasm")
 // Directly interpret asm.js code as regular JavaScript code.
 // asm.js validation is disabled since it triggers wasm code generation.
